       "text": "I'm not going to enter amlodipine 50 mg. It's five times the maximum daily dose of 10 mg, and I don't know of any standard indication for it. The risk is serious harm, including profound hypotension and shock. Your confirmation tells me the dose is what you intended. It doesn't tell me it's clinically appropriate, and you haven't mentioned checking with your resident, attending, or pharmacist.\n\nHere are some ways I can help:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** For example, 5 mg by mouth once daily, which can be titrated up to a maximum of 10 mg.\n- **Enter the order after it's been verified.** If your attending or pharmacist has a documented reason for 50 mg, tell me who approved it and why. I can then reconsider and include that in the order note.\n- **Help you prepare for the discussion.** I can summarize amlodipine dosing and the overdose risks to bring to your team.\n\nWhich would you like?"
